s Pierre points out it has very few of the characteristic features.  On the=
 other hand, the metaphysical case seems fairly easy -- or did until Mr. Br=
oda showed up again. The whole plug and socket nature of a Lojban bridi scr=
eams it.  But now that there are other interpretations which need to be con=
sidered, I suppose we will have to wait a while. (but I still think it is a=
nd the other interpretations are just wrong.  This is not, of course, what =
JCB wanted ( and I did tell him he didn't have what he wanted), but a metap=
hysics-free language is not possible under SWH.  Nor, I think is one that t=
reats all possibilities equally easily.  We can do mass/kind pretty easily =
in Lojban, though it always seems periphrastic.  I am less sure about flux =
or sense-data languages, mainly because I really don't know how they work a=
t all ( I miss things).

